      "path": "lcnc-gateway/lcnc_trace.py",
      "sha256": "968e2542040fc5ee760beed625d58520cb0e5200a15baa57bebb61a2b81552b4",
      "excerpts": [
        {
          "start": 1,
          "end": 31,
          "lines": [
            "1: \"\"\"Suite-wide structured trace bus.",
            "2: ",
            "3: Every component (gateway, hal_reader, hal_watchdog) imports this module and",
            "4: calls `init(<proc_name>)` once at startup, then `emit(tag, **fields)` for",
            "5: each event. All events land in trace.ndjson under the resolved log dir",
            "6: (see lcnc_paths.resolve(); default <install-dir>/runlogs).",
            "7: ",
            "8: Why one shared file across processes: Linux guarantees atomic O_APPEND writes",
            "9: up to PIPE_BUF (4096 B), so concurrent appends from multiple processes are",
            "10: line-atomic (emit() caps each line below that). Each line carries `proc` + `pid`",
            "11: so the bundler can demux later.",
            "12: ",
            "13: Known limitation — multi-writer rollover: the four writers each hold their own",
            "14: fd and size-check independently, so plain RotatingFileHandler can race at the",
            "15: 50 MB rollover boundary (two processes rename trace.ndjson->.1 at once, losing",
            "16: history, or one keeps appending to a rotated-away fd). This is accepted as a",
            "17: rare, diagnostic-only risk: it needs the file to hit 50 MB AND two processes to",
            "18: cross within the same sub-ms window, and the cost is lost forensic history at a",
            "19: rotation boundary — never a control/safety effect. The clean fixes both have a",
            "20: worse cost here: concurrent-log-handler's portalocker lock only coordinates if",
            "21: EVERY writer holds it, but the HAL siblings run under the system python (no",
            "22: venv access), so it would be dead weight; a stdlib fcntl.flock handler would",
            "23: work but is custom code in the trace path. If rollover corruption is ever",
            "24: actually observed, the flock handler is the dependency-free way to close it.",
            "25: ",
            "26: Why direct file write (not queue + thread): NDJSON encoding is < 50 us per",
            "27: event; line-buffered O_APPEND write is 1-10 us uncached. At our event rate",
            "28: (~50/s steady, ~500/s burst) the cost is negligible vs the asyncio loop's",
            "29: heartbeat budget.",
            "30: ",
            "31: Format example:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 124,
          "end": 135,
          "lines": [
